{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794589657606,"sessionID":"ses_e2a221671ffeX23N5SliezE5hI","part":{"partID":"prt_1d5e105e4001KsdNHbjsvjIcM2","sessionID":"ses_e2a221671ffeX23N5SliezE5hI","messageID":"msg_1d5e0f7bd001gJHvZ6x0WoAR95","type":"tool","id":"call_be451a226b18435e8ce95045","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"git -c core.fsmonitor=false status --porcelain -- .skilled/commands/doctor; echo \"--- diff ---\"; git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff -- .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-embed.yaml .skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml | head -60","workdir":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research"},"output":" M .skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml\n M .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-embed.yaml\n M .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs\n M .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/doctor-agents-md-contract.test.cjs\n M .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/hook-wiring-check.test.cjs\n--- diff ---\ndiff --git a/.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml b/.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml\nindex 1f42e5c59d..92cad1721a 100644\n--- a/.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml\n+++ b/.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml\n@@ -543,7 +543,7 @@ routes:\n     setup_vars: [execution_mode, root, dry_run, plan_digest, digest_confirmation, keep_claude_md, create_router]\n     allowed_flags: [\"--dry-run\", \"--root <dir>\", \"--plan-digest <digest>\", \"--keep-claude-md\", \"--remove-claude-md\", \"--create-router\"]\n     mutating: mutates\n-    gate3_location: \"AGENTS.md (created when absent, replaced with the shipped sections plus the composed block), CLAUDE.md and .codex/AGENTS.md (folded into the block and removed, unless --keep-claude-md), .cursor/rules/repo-local.md (the generated mirror of a non-empty block) and REPO RULES.md (missing shipped rows appended, or the file created behind --create-router), with a copy of every touched path taken to the plan's backup folder under .skilled/output/doctor-agents-md/<timestamp>/ before the first byte, and .cursor/rules/skill-routing.md rewritten by the pointer generator the engine calls; the write runs only against the plan digest the operator approved\"\n+    gate3_location: \"AGENTS.md (created when absent, replaced with the shipped sections plus the composed block), CLAUDE.md and .codex/AGENTS.md (folded into the block and removed, unless --keep-claude-md), .cursor/rules/repo-local.md (the generated mirror of a non-empty block) and REPO RULES.md (missing shipped rows appended, or the file created behind --create-router), with a copy of every touched path taken to the plan's backup folder, .skilled/output/doctor-agents-md/<first 16 characters of the plan digest>/ or the folder of that name under the operating system's temporary directory when git does not ignore that path, before the first byte, and .cursor/rules/skill-routing.md rewritten by the pointer generator the engine calls; the write runs only against the plan digest the operator approved\"\n     mcp_tools: []   # script-only; no MCP calls\n     script_invocations:\n       - 'node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs plan  # read-only: composes every target in memory and prints the targets, the diffs, the block, the budget, the preservation ledger, the backup folder and the plan digest; the workflow adds --root <dir>, --keep-claude-md, --create-router and --dry-run only when the operator passed them'\ndiff --git a/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-embed.yaml b/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-embed.yaml\nindex 6fe597d842..9aef52b6fe 100644\n--- a/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-embed.yaml\n+++ b/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-embed.yaml\n@@ -31,7 +31,7 @@ mutation_boundaries:\n     - \".cursor/rules/repo-local.md, the generated mirror of a non-empty block; removed when the block is empty\"\n     - \".cursor/rules/skill-routing.md, rewritten by its own generator, sync-gate1-pointers.cjs, which this engine calls and never composes a byte of\"\n     - \"REPO RULES.md, the router: shipped rows that are missing are appended and no other row is touched, and a missing file is created only behind --create-router\"\n-    - \"the backup directory the plan prints, .skilled/output/doctor-agents-md/<timestamp>/ or the operating system's temporary directory when git does not ignore that path: every path the run touches is copied there before the first write, and the record beside the copies is what restore reads\"\n+    - \"the backup directory the plan prints, .skilled/output/doctor-agents-md/<first 16 characters of the plan digest>/ or the operating system's temporary directory when git does not ignore that path: every path the run touches is copied there before the first write, and the record beside the copies is what restore reads\"\n   forbidden_targets:\n     - \"any path outside that allowlist, which the engine checks in code before every write rather than trusting this document\"\n     - \".skilled/**, which /doctor:update owns, including the manifest this engine reads\"\n@@ -101,7 +101,7 @@ workflow:\n       - \"Exit 0 means the write ran. Keep exactly the lines the engine printed: its apply line, one wrote or removed line per path, the pointer-sync line, the repo-rules line after a router write, the preservation line, the check-after line, the backup line, the undo line, one copy line per overwritten file and STATUS=OK.\"\n       - \"A nonzero pointer-sync line is the one verdict the run leaves unresolved: the generator rewrites an existing .cursor/rules/skill-routing.md and never creates a missing one, so a repository without that file ends with exit 1 and the mirror still missing. Keep the line as printed, render it in the result's Pointer sync: field, never list .cursor/rules/skill-routing.md in Files changed on the strength of the allowlist that names it, and render a Next: line naming /doctor:runtime-mirrors, whose rows list each generated mirror that drifts with the write form of its checker. The repair chain for the pointer file itself is the presentation's troubleshooting row for A10, because that route does not check it. A repo-rules line that reports an error belongs in Router: the same way.\"\n       - \"Exit 1 means the proof found a dropped line or a `foreign:` line. The engine restored from the backup by itself unless it printed `nothing was restored`, and kept the backup. Quote the lines the proof named, then STATUS=FAIL, and say the tree is as the plan found it when the restore ran. Never repair a file by hand inside this route.\"\n-      - \"Exit 3 means a write failed after the backup. When the output holds restored:, the engine put every recorded path back: quote the ERROR line, show the backup and undo lines, end with STATUS=FAIL and say the tree is as the plan found it. When it holds nothing was restored, the tree is as the failed write left it: show the backup and undo lines, end with STATUS=FAIL and name the undo command as the next step.\"\n+      - \"Exit 3 means a write failed after the backup. When the output holds restored:, the engine put every recorded path back: quote the ERROR line, show the backup and undo lines, end with STATUS=FAIL and say the tree is as the plan found it. When it holds nothing was restored, the tree is as the failed write left it: show the backup and undo lines, end with STATUS=FAIL and name the undo command as the next step. When it holds ERROR: the restore failed, the restore itself threw and the tree may be partly written: quote both ERROR lines, show the backup and undo lines, end with STATUS=FAIL and name the undo command as the next step. This outcome takes precedence over the restored: outcome.\"\n       - \"An allowlist refusal exits 2 before a backup exists, because every path the run would touch is resolved before the first byte. Quote the message and end with STATUS=FAIL. Nothing was written.\"\n \n   phase_5_reread:\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":" M .skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml\n M .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-embed.yaml\n M .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs\n M .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/doctor-agents-md-contract.test.cjs\n M .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/hook-wiring-check.test.cjs\n--- diff ---\ndiff --git a/.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml b/.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml\nindex 1f42e5c59d..92cad1721a 100644\n--- a/.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml\n+++ b/.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml\n@@ -543,7 +543,7 @@ routes:\n     setup_vars: [execution_mode, root, dry_run, plan_digest, digest_confirmation, keep_claude_md, create_router]\n     allowed_flags: [\"--dry-run\", \"--root <dir>\", \"--plan-digest <digest>\", \"--keep-claude-md\", \"--remove-claude-md\", \"--create-router\"]\n     mutating: mutates\n-    gate3_location: \"AGENTS.md (created when absent, replaced with the shipped sections plus the composed block), CLAUDE.md and .codex/AGENTS.md (folded into the block and removed, unless --keep-claude-md), .cursor/rules/repo-local.md (the generated mirror of a non-empty block) and REPO RULES.md (missing shipped rows appended, or the file created behind --create-router), with a copy of every touched path taken to the plan's backup folder under .skilled/output/doctor-agents-md/<timestamp>/ before the first byte, and .cursor/rules/skill-routing.md rewritten by the pointer generator the engine calls; the write runs only against the plan digest the operator approved\"\n+    gate3_location: \"AGENTS.md (created when absent, replaced with the shipped sections plus the composed block), CLAUDE.md and .codex/AGENTS.md (folded into the block and removed, unless --keep-claude-md), .cursor/rules/repo-local.md (the generated mirror of a non-empty block) and REPO RULES.md (missing shipped rows appended, or the file created behind --create-router), with a copy of every touched path taken to the plan's backup folder, .skilled/output/doctor-agents-md/<first 16 characters of the plan digest>/ or the folder of that name under the operating system's temporary directory when git does not ignore that path, before the first byte, and .cursor/rules/skill-routing.md rewritten by the pointer generator the engine calls; the write runs only against the plan digest the operator approved\"\n     mcp_tools: []   # script-only; no MCP calls\n     script_invocations:\n       - 'node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs plan  # read-only: composes every target in memory and prints the targets, the diffs, the block, the budget, the preservation ledger, the backup folder and the plan digest; the workflow adds --root <dir>, --keep-claude-md, --create-router and --dry-run only when the operator passed them'\ndiff --git a/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-embed.yaml b/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-embed.yaml\nindex 6fe597d842..9aef52b6fe 100644\n--- a/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-embed.yaml\n+++ b/.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-embed.yaml\n@@ -31,7 +31,7 @@ mutation_boundaries:\n     - \".cursor/rules/repo-local.md, the generated mirror of a non-empty block; removed when the block is empty\"\n     - \".cursor/rules/skill-routing.md, rewritten by its own generator, sync-gate1-pointers.cjs, which this engine calls and never composes a byte of\"\n     - \"REPO RULES.md, the router: shipped rows that are missing are appended and no other row is touched, and a missing file is created only behind --create-router\"\n-    - \"the backup directory the plan prints, .skilled/output/doctor-agents-md/<timestamp>/ or the operating system's temporary directory when git does not ignore that path: every path the run touches is copied there before the first write, and the record beside the copies is what restore reads\"\n+    - \"the backup directory the plan prints, .skilled/output/doctor-agents-md/<first 16 characters of the plan digest>/ or the operating system's temporary directory when git does not ignore that path: every path the run touches is copied there before the first write, and the record beside the copies is what restore reads\"\n   forbidden_targets:\n     - \"any path outside that allowlist, which the engine checks in code before every write rather than trusting this document\"\n     - \".skilled/**, which /doctor:update owns, including the manifest this engine reads\"\n@@ -101,7 +101,7 @@ workflow:\n       - \"Exit 0 means the write ran. Keep exactly the lines the engine printed: its apply line, one wrote or removed line per path, the pointer-sync line, the repo-rules line after a router write, the preservation line, the check-after line, the backup line, the undo line, one copy line per overwritten file and STATUS=OK.\"\n       - \"A nonzero pointer-sync line is the one verdict the run leaves unresolved: the generator rewrites an existing .cursor/rules/skill-routing.md and never creates a missing one, so a repository without that file ends with exit 1 and the mirror still missing. Keep the line as printed, render it in the result's Pointer sync: field, never list .cursor/rules/skill-routing.md in Files changed on the strength of the allowlist that names it, and render a Next: line naming /doctor:runtime-mirrors, whose rows list each generated mirror that drifts with the write form of its checker. The repair chain for the pointer file itself is the presentation's troubleshooting row for A10, because that route does not check it. A repo-rules line that reports an error belongs in Router: the same way.\"\n       - \"Exit 1 means the proof found a dropped line or a `foreign:` line. The engine restored from the backup by itself unless it printed `nothing was restored`, and kept the backup. Quote the lines the proof named, then STATUS=FAIL, and say the tree is as the plan found it when the restore ran. Never repair a file by hand inside this route.\"\n-      - \"Exit 3 means a write failed after the backup. When the output holds restored:, the engine put every recorded path back: quote the ERROR line, show the backup and undo lines, end with STATUS=FAIL and say the tree is as the plan found it. When it holds nothing was restored, the tree is as the failed write left it: show the backup and undo lines, end with STATUS=FAIL and name the undo command as the next step.\"\n+      - \"Exit 3 means a write failed after the backup. When the output holds restored:, the engine put every recorded path back: quote the ERROR line, show the backup and undo lines, end with STATUS=FAIL and say the tree is as the plan found it. When it holds nothing was restored, the tree is as the failed write left it: show the backup and undo lines, end with STATUS=FAIL and name the undo command as the next step. When it holds ERROR: the restore failed, the restore itself threw and the tree may be partly written: quote both ERROR lines, show the backup and undo lines, end with STATUS=FAIL and name the undo command as the next step. This outcome takes precedence over the restored: outcome.\"\n       - \"An allowlist refusal exits 2 before a backup exists, because every path the run would touch is resolved before the first byte. Quote the message and end with STATUS=FAIL. Nothing was written.\"\n \n   phase_5_reread:\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"git -c core.fsmonitor=false status --porcelain -- .skilled/commands/doctor; echo \\\"--- diff ---\\\"; git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff -- .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-agents-md-embed.yaml .skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml | head -60\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research\"}"},"time":{"start":1794589656548,"end":1794589657606}}}}
